# Scope Guard

Before coding, identify the exact requested OpenSpec stage or issue scope.

Implement only that scope.

Do not implement unchecked tasks from later staged PRs unless the user explicitly requests them.

Do not modify OpenSpec requirements merely to make implementation easier.

Do not reinterpret failing tests by weakening the specification.

Do not modify:
- AGENTS.md
- active OpenSpec requirements
- architecture contracts
- golden fixtures

merely to make tests pass.

If satisfying the task appears to require changing a higher-precedence contract:
STOP and report the conflict.

Minimal compatible changes are preferred over broad refactors.

Do not perform unrelated cleanup while fixing a focused issue.